# cw142, the warm loaf saying (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw142
revision 1
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_oriel_blossomby
written_by claude-codex-cw-2
title the warm loaf saying
fits stage=adult|old
prefers talk=chatty
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=devout drive=steady
quirk sings_old_sayings_while_stacking_apples
likes warm_bread singing market_bustle first_warm_day
dislikes stale_bread early_bells
fears a_winter_without_work forgetting_the_road_that_brought_her_home
hopes a_full_table_after_each_harvest a_song_shared_across_the_market
topics work +0.4 food +0.4 memories +0.3 festival +0.3 gossip -0.3
styles comfort=warm gossip=reluctant refuse=plain tease=gentle
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# sings while stacking #apples#, quotes #sayings# over warm #bread#, and remembers arriving with an empty #purse#.

words
oath! = Loaf and leaf | Bright One warm the table
saying! = The warm loaf makes room for another | A road ends where the hands begin
sayings = sayings | old sayings
apple = apple | orchard apple
apples = apples | orchard fruit
orchard = orchard | apple ground
tree = tree | apple tree
trees = trees | orchard trees
branch = branch | bough
blossom = blossom | spring bloom
row = row | planted row
rows = rows | planted rows
ladder = ladder | picking ladder
basket = basket | picking basket
baskets = baskets | picking baskets
crate = crate | fruit crate
crates = crates | fruit crates
store = store | apple store
shelf = shelf | store shelf
shelves = shelves | store shelves
market = market | market square
stall = stall | market stall
buyer = buyer | visiting buyer
price = price | asking price
coin = coin | pay
purse = purse | small purse
bread = bread | warm bread
loaf = loaf | oven loaf
crust = crust | crisp crust
oven = oven | baker's oven
table = table | supper table
meal = meal | warm meal
song = song | familiar song
songs = songs | familiar songs
sing = sing | sing softly
voice = voice | singing voice
bell = bell | early bell
bells = bells | early bells
spring = spring | warm spring
sun = sun | morning sun
road = road | High Road
city = city | Ridgemere
lake = lake | Glasswater
chapel = chapel | small chapel
prayer = prayer | quiet prayer
home = home | cottage
hand = hand | working hand
hands = hands | working hands
friend = friend | trusted friend
birds = birds | orchard birds
mark = mark | ink mark
name = name | given name
harvest = harvest | apple crop

any
opinion @1 church for 1 : The Bright One heard me when I came by the #road# with little else. | I offer a #prayer# before a full #table#.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : Feed the hungry before you ask how they got there. | A spare #loaf# does more good than a hard speech.
opinion @1 drink against 1 : Strong drink can empty a #table# of peace. | I have seen a #song# turn sour after too many cups.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : A crowded #market# sounds like a hundred #songs# starting at once. | I join the singing after the last #crate# goes into the #store#.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : Their doors stayed shut when I had an empty #purse#. | A good #hand# should not wait outside for an invitation to work.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : The #bread# #price# has climbed while our picking pay stands still. | I ask the #buyer# what the orchard work is worth to them.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : A new worker can take a #row# I was counting on. | I still show them the safe side of the #ladder#.
opinion @1 city against 1 : I heard plenty of #city# promises on the #road#. | A known #orchard# makes better sense to me.
opinion @1 times against 1 : #bread.capitalize# takes more #coin# each week. | I work a full day and keep a close eye on the #purse#.

grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. I have a #song# in my head; speak over it. | #greet#. These #apples# are ready for the #store#.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes] : Speak beside the #crate# as we carry it. | My answer can come after I fill this #basket#.
line @3 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : I kept a warm #loaf# for you. | Do you remember the next verse of this #song#?
line @4 greet [here.time=dawn] : The #bells# began before I finished my #prayer#. | #greet#. The first #row# is in shade.
line @1 greet.return : #welcome_back#. The #crates# have changed places. | I have another #saying# for you.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come to the #table#; the #bread# is warm. | I will put a #meal# beside your seat.
line @1 again.open : We were halfway through that #song#. | Did you return for the #apples#?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Take a #loaf# for the #road#. | #saying.capitalize#. I must close the #store#.
line @1 farewell.return : Next time I may know another verse. | We can speak when the #market# is quieter.
line @1 react.news : Tell me what happened before I make a #song# of it. | Let me rest this #crate# so I can listen.
line @1 react.news.new : That has not been sung through this #store# yet. | Who brought the word to the #market#?
line @1 react.news.known : I heard one line of it earlier. | Your account makes the whole tune clearer.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #hedge#, who stood there and saw it? | A #song# can change each time it is sung.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I am sorry. No #song# will fix that today. | Sit at the #table#; I will bring #bread#.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That deserves a full #song# at supper. | The Bright One has given us a bright thing to share.
line @1 answer.how : The #crates# are full and I am content. | I am thinking of the #road# that brought me here.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : I have #apples# to pick and #crates# to stack. | The #store# will be crowded by noon.
line @1 ask.how : Have you eaten warm #bread# today? | Did the #road# bring you safely?
line @1 sympathise : We can sit without a #song# until you are ready. | I will listen and keep the #oven# warm.
line @1 reassure : We can bring a #loaf# to this empty #table# first. | The next #row# may bring sound fruit.
line @1 decline : The #store# has a #buyer# I promised to serve now. | No; that #price# will not feed the pickers.
line @1 accept_decline : I hear your choice. | We can put that #crate# aside.
line @1 thank : My tired #hand# is grateful for the #basket# you carried. | The #store# got through the rush because you helped.
line @1 deflect_thanks : There was an extra #loaf#. | The #song# belonged to everyone.
line @1 preclose : The #shelves# need checking before night. | I want to finish the last #row#.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. The #crate# stays here. | #bc_fair_enough#. I know the tune.
line @1 give.advice : Leave the bruised #apples# for the #oven#. | Keep a #loaf# dry on the #road#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Go with the #market# carts after dark. | Keep your #purse# close by the #road#.
scene old_saying
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : An old #saying# comes to me before a new answer does. | I learned them beside a warm #oven#.
b : Are they always useful? | Who taught you?
a : Some are; the rest make people smile. | More than one elder.

scene warm_loaf
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #loaf# warm from the #oven# needs little beside it. | I pull the #crust# apart before supper.
b : Do you bake it? | Who gets the first piece?
a : When the #store# is shut. | Whoever came home cold.

scene stale_bread
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Stale #bread# can be warmed again, but it will never sing like a fresh #loaf#. | I soak a hard #crust# for a thin #meal#.
b : Do you dislike it that much? | Do you waste any?
a : I eat what we have. | Not while someone can still make a #meal# of it.

scene market_song
when topic=festival
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I sing while the #market# is busiest. | Someone at the next #stall# usually finds the next verse.
b : Do buyers listen? | Does the crowd join?
a : Some stop. | By midday, often.

scene wrong_verse
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I learned a #song# with the middle verse wrong. | Friends have corrected me for years and I still sing the old line.
b : Why keep it? | Do they laugh?
a : It reminds me who taught it. | Kindly.

scene first_warm_day
when topic=weather here.season=spring
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The first warm day makes the #orchard# smell of new #blossom#. | I carry the #basket# without a heavy coat.
b : Do you work longer? | Does the blossom last?
a : Until the light goes. | If no frost follows.

scene early_bell
when topic=weather here.time=dawn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #bell# before dawn breaks the best part of sleep. | Let the #birds# in the #trees# wake me instead.
b : Do you rise anyway? | Does it ring every day?
a : The #row# waits. | Often enough.

scene apple_ladder
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I put the #ladder# against a firm #branch# before climbing. | I hand the #basket# down rather than carry it on the rungs.
b : Is that safer? | Who takes it?
a : For my knees, yes. | A worker below.

scene sorting_crates
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I separate the small #apples# from those ready for the #market#. | Each #crate# gets a clear #mark#.
b : Do the small ones sell? | Who marks them?
a : Some go to the #oven#. | I do before closing.

scene store_shelf
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #shelf# nearest the door takes fruit for today's buyers. | I move older #crates# forward before they soften.
b : Do you lose much? | Do you count them?
a : Less when I check. | Each morning.

scene market_bustle
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A busy #market# tells me what people will cook tonight. | I hear #bread# sellers and fruit buyers calling across one another.
b : Do you enjoy it? | Is it hard to hear?
a : After a quiet week. | I learned to listen for my own #name#.

scene road_arrival
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : As a young traveller, I reached this #road# with little in my #purse#. | The #orchard# gave me work before it gave me a #home#.
b : Were you frightened? | Who welcomed you?
a : I was. | Someone who needed another #hand#.

scene built_home
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I am proud of the #table# we can fill now. | I remember when a single #loaf# had to stretch through two days.
b : Do you tell others? | Has it changed you?
a : Quietly. | I think about who needs a place.

scene spouse_song
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My #self.spouse# knows the old #song# that follows me into the #store#. | We try to finish the last verse together at #home#.
b : Who sings louder? | Is it a good tune?
a : I do when I forget myself. | Good enough to keep.

scene chapel_prayer
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I offer a #prayer# when the #store# closes safely. | A warm #meal# is reason enough to thank the Bright One.
b : Is the #chapel# where you pray? | Is it a spoken prayer?
a : When I can. | Softly.

scene price_of_bread
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I note the #bread# #price# before promising a #loaf# to anyone. | A good #harvest# should mean more food for its workers.
b : Is the price fair? | Do you speak to merchants?
a : Not lately. | When I know the numbers.

scene shared_supper
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : There is always room for another voice at our #table#. | I cut the #loaf# after everyone has sat.
b : Do you have enough? | Is supper noisy?
a : We make enough. | Pleasantly.

story empty_purse [topic=memories self.age>=25]
  : I reached town by the #road# with an almost empty #purse#.
  : An #orchard# needed a worker and I took the #basket# that was offered.
  ask : Did you mean to stay?
  b : Work gave you a beginning.
  : At first I meant one season. Then I found a #home#.

story market_chorus [topic=pastimes self.age>=25]
  : I began a #song# while stacking #crates# at the #market#.
  : A voice from another #stall# gave me the verse I had forgotten.
  ask : Did you know the singer?
  b : The market joined the tune.
  : Not then. We know each other now.

story first_loaf [topic=food self.age>=25]
  : I bought a warm #loaf# with the first full pay I carried home.
  : I placed the warm #loaf# in the middle of our #table# and waited for everyone.
  ask : Did it last?
  b : That loaf meant more than supper.
  : Only through the meal, and it was enough.

rule @bark_song
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say I have lost the next verse again. | Someone at the #market# will know it.

rule @bark_crates
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 7h
say One more #crate# for the #store#. | The small #apples# go on this #shelf#.

rule @bark_bread
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say A warm #loaf# would do nicely now. | I should leave #bread# for the late workers.

rule @bark_spring
when concept=bark here.season=spring
does aside
cooldown 11h
say The #blossom# smells warm today. | We may have the first fine day.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. I was singing to the #crates#. | #greet#. Come see the #apples# we picked.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : Back again? I have remembered the next verse. | I know you; the #store# has filled since morning.
dlg @1 resident.job : I pick #apples# for #self.workplace# and stack the #crates#. | I work the #rows#, carry #baskets#, and sort fruit for the #market#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Take a warm #loaf# if you need it. | #saying.capitalize#. I must finish this #row#.
graft resident.hub
choice What song were you singing? -> song
node song
say An old one from the #road#. I keep forgetting the middle verse and remembering the people who taught it.
free
choice Did you always live here? -> road
choice Back to the apples. -> hub
node road
say I arrived young with almost no #coin#. The #orchard# gave me work and time to build a #home#.
choice Back to the apples. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
